    <main>
      <section class="intro" aria-label="About me">
        <p>
          I am an economics researcher whose interests lie in <strong>health economics, family economics, and applied microeconomics.</strong>  I am an Economics PhD Candidate at the <strong>University of Exeter</strong>.
        </p>
        <p>
          I am currently a <strong>Postdoc Research Fellow</strong> at Bayes Business School, City St George's, University of London, where I work in the <strong>Impact Evaluation of Virtual Wards Project</strong>.
        </p>
        <p>
          My main research focuses on topics related to (i) healthcare systems, health care delivery and health policy; (ii) measurement and dynamics of norms; (iii) bidimensional marriage matching models and role of norms in marriage matching; and (iv) other broader topics in family economics and applied microeconomics including fertility decisions, human capital investment, and sex selection.
          <!-- I study healthcare systems, marriage matching, and gender norms, using
          quasi-experimental methods and evidence from administrative records,
          household surveys, and biomarkers. -->
        </p>
        <p>
